# Intent: open the camera and avatar socket in AI-agent mode (owner report 2026-10-21: the unit cannot say what it sees; the host log shows "StackChan camera stream could not start ... avatar channel is not connected" on every connect and "0 frames" every minute). Root cause: the avatar websocket client is a Mooncake ability (WebsocketAvatarWorker) that only AppAvatar::onOpen creates, and the firmware boots straight into the voice agent without Mooncake apps (main.cpp skips them), so the avatar socket was never opened; the host comment says as much ("AI-agent mode never starts it"). This runs the same worker from a plain task once the voice agent reports ready (first STANDBY), and turns the avatar address that the enroll image stores (http://host:port) into ws://host:port, since the websocket client needs a ws scheme. It starts only if an avatar address is saved and at least 32 KB of internal RAM is free for the task stack and client; otherwise it stays off and says why (avatar_channel event). The host sends faces over the voice socket (this firmware has no expression handler on the avatar socket in agent mode) and uses the avatar socket for the camera only.
# Upstream: m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/hal_ws_avatar.cpp, hal.h, hal/board/stackchan_display.cc (MIT). Applies after 053 with --unidiff-zero.
# Check after a flash: the host log shows "unit touch: avatar_channel state=started" (or state=off with why=ram and the free bytes), no "avatar channel is not connected" after that, and "StackChan camera: N frames" with N above 0 once the camera stream starts.
